==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Henry]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07~4 seconds<sup>2f~120f</sup>.
**30 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07~2 seconds<sup>2f~60f</sup>.
**3 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Meatshields, very good [[Cat Combo|Combos]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] can do it easily, better if you add a good [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] or [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] cat such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]].

Keep in mind that there's plenty of money, so go with spammable cats rather than cost-efficient ones (in other words, no [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bath Cat]]): a stack of Cyborgs can make quick work of the Doge Darks like they were simple [[Doge]]s.

If you have him, [[Hattori Hanzo (Uber Rare Cat)|Hattori Hanzo]] can be an excellent addition to your lineup, as he is able to [[Freeze]] and deal [[Massive Damage]] the Doge Darks and Shy Boys, while being immune to Henry's Freeze.

==Trivia==
*Deadly Weapons's Japanese name, Gachigachi Ankoku Heiki (ガチガチ暗黒兵器, "Rigid Dark Weapon"), is the opposite of [[Fluffy Dark Weapon]].

